WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.7 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Culture, wellbeing and inclusion

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Culture forms in the first months, mostly from what founders do, so build it on purpose.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.504
Culture is what people actually do when no one is checking: how decisions are made, how mistakes are handled, how people disagree and whose voice counts. It forms in the first months, mostly from what founders do.

4
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.504
Three parts to build on purpose

5
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:40.463
Everyday habits: How decisions, mistakes and disagreements are handled, linked to your values. For example: At our bakery, every failed batch is discussed openly as a lesson, never blamed.

6
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:51.793
Wellbeing: Reasonable workload limits, modelled by founders, and support when work is distressing. For example: The bakery founders send no work messages after 8 pm, and keep to it.

7
00:00:51.793 --> 00:01:03.952
Inclusion and voice: Accessibility, language, meeting times, caring duties, and safety to speak up. For example: The bakery sets shifts around bus times so trainees from further away can join.

8
00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:04.952
Why it matters

9
00:01:04.952 --> 00:01:09.885
1. Culture either supports your values or quietly contradicts them.

10
00:01:09.885 --> 00:01:15.559
2. Founders are often the first to burn out in purpose-led work.

11
00:01:15.559 --> 00:01:22.233
3. Speaking up safely is the basis for learning and for safeguarding.

12
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.233
What it connects to

13
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:28.167
1. Your values from Module 1, turned into daily practice.

14
00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:33.470
2. Your check-ins and, as you grow, a short anonymous survey.

15
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:39.774
3. Your safeguarding approach: people raise concerns because they feel safe.

16
00:01:40.174 --> 00:01:40.774
What to avoid

17
00:01:40.774 --> 00:01:44.596
Justifying long hours with the mission.

18
00:01:44.596 --> 00:01:49.159
Stating values that the founders do not live.

19
00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:55.833
Asking how people are, then not acting on what you hear.

20
00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:58.233
You describe three culture practices and how you will check them.

21
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:02.233
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:06.833
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
